From: Tetris port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: provide a disabled Tetris CCCI metadata consumer

The metadata-only U-Boot profile publishes owned AP tags only to an existing,
sole disabled mediatek,mddriver consumer. The Tetris base DT currently lacks
one, so the real final publisher refuses without publishing a descriptor.

Retain the compatible, AP platform and MD generation from Nothing B4.1
device modules ee2be53cb75670b548948636a0db1d1ff112bf12, mt6878.dts.
This is only a disabled metadata anchor: it has no registers, interrupts,
power/clock consumers or inherited CCCI descriptor. Do not enable it as an
operational modem; those physical resources still need their own integration.
Native display and diagnostic variants inherit the same single anchor.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts
@@ -15,6 +15,14 @@
 	#address-cells = <2>;
 	#size-cells = <2>;
 
+	/* Metadata only; runtime transport remains disabled. */
+	mddriver: modem {
+		compatible = "mediatek,mddriver";
+		mediatek,ap-plat-info = <6878>;
+		mediatek,md-generation = <6299>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+
 	aliases {
 		serial0 = &uart0;
 	};
